 "purpose": "The sentence parser input object (Taal › Zinsdelen): shows a sentence as word blocks and lets the child mark the parts of the sentence step by step or by free colouring.",
 "details": "ZinsdelenInvoer plugs into terminal/oefenaar.py through INVOER['zinsdelen'] and builds on StappenHulp (tips, cheat sheet, second-chance switches). Steps come from kern/taal/zinsontleding.py (pv, o, wwg/nwg, lv, mv, bwb, and optionally 'verdelen' first). Modes: step by step (default), free colouring with letter keys (Tab toggles; on Moeilijk free colouring is on from the start) and, for a sentence with several finite verbs, a special 'pick all pv' step. All checking is done in kern (Z.nakijken, Z.nakijken_vrij, Z.nakijken_verdeling, Z.diagnose); the object only collects the selection and shows messages. A sentence counts as correct if every part is correct, even after the second chance (then it enters the repeat bin). At the end it returns ('juist'/'fout') as the answer and fills `extra` and `uitleg_na`.",
 "module_docstring": "De zinsontleder: een zin als woordblokjes, de zinsdelen aanduiden (Taal, docs/taal.md). Een invoer-object voor terminal/oefenaar.py, zoals het vraagstuk (eigen_tekst, eigen_tip, extra, uitleg_na).",
